@page "/docs/components/scroll-area"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.ScrollArea
<PageTitle>Scroll Area - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Scroll Area</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="scroll-area" />
        </div>
        <p>A scrollable region that hides the native scrollbar and draws a slim, themed thumb over the content instead, so the scrollbar takes no layout space. The thumb tracks the scroll position, can be dragged, and shows only when you choose: on overflow, always, on hover or while scrolling.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ScrollAreaUsageExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, wrap the content in a `BzScrollArea` and size the root through `Class`. The vertical scrollbar appears when the content overflows." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="A fixed-height region that scrolls vertically, with the overlay scrollbar shown whenever the content overflows." Example="typeof(ScrollAreaDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Horizontal" Description="Set `Orientation` to `Horizontal` for a row that scrolls sideways. Lay the content out as a row that does not wrap, such as a `w-max` flex container." Example="typeof(ScrollAreaHorizontalExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Both axes" Description="With `Orientation` set to `Both`, each axis gets its own scrollbar with a corner where they meet. Use it for content that is both wide and tall, such as a data grid." Example="typeof(ScrollAreaBothExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Visibility" Description="`Behavior` controls when the scrollbar shows. `Auto` shows it whenever the content overflows and `Always` keeps it visible, while `Hover` shows it on pointer hover or while scrolling and `Scroll` only while scrolling, fading afterwards." Example="typeof(ScrollAreaTypeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization" Description="Size the region with `Class` on the root, and restyle the thumb by targeting its `data-slot`. This example uses a wider indigo thumb on a tinted surface." Example="typeof(ScrollAreaCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the vertical scrollbar moves to the left edge and the content flows from right to left." Example="typeof(ScrollAreaRtlExample)" />

</div>

